what has it been like to sort of reach  this new level  of stardom and what's been i guess the  best part and what's been the hardest  part for you  i think the best part has just been the  people that i've met and the connections  i've made the friendships that i have  now and like are continuing to  get are like such deep and fun  and loving relationships i think the  hardest part  would probably be like just i guess the  negativity  i feel like that's a pretty common  answer but i think just dealing with you  know  the fact that there are just going to be  people that don't like you and  will always have something negative to  say about you and i think a big part of  that too was just kind of dealing with  like  the pressures of being so talked about  on the internet  at a time because it's like that's when  the negativity is the strongest  and it's like body image and you know  just things like that were really hard  for me to handle at first because i  wasn't used to that and it's like  now um i like noticed myself  getting like super hard on myself about  it and like letting that get to me and  it's kind of just um a part of growing  through it and just being like  look this is who i am this is who i was  meant to be and i can't let people that  don't truly know  the real me in my heart you know and  haven't met me  kind of determine how i feel about  myself so that's been the hardest part  but  there's so many good parts about this  industry and the social media world that  like  it kind of just outweighs it speaking of  the negative comments i love that you  sort of put this body shamer in her  place  i just feel like everyone needs to know  that like bullying  and body shaming is not acceptable and  not  okay mom for you what was it like to see  her getting that negative  commentary on her post and was there  like a conversation that you guys had  about that i feel like this is a good  learning experience for other young  girls out there  no for sure yeah it's definitely hard  for a mom to see  those things and try to explain to her  a lot of people are struggling  themselves with with issues  and to not take those things  and hold them in to talk about them  to get it out like if something is  bothering her and  she's struggling with the negative  comments also try not to listen to them  try to let it go after you've talked  about it  just let it go and don't hold it to  these people  they're they're behind a computer screen  they're we don't know what they're going  through  themselves yeah and i think for me too  that's what i've told myself forever is  just like  like my entire life of course has always  been negativity no matter what and like  you always  go through something that you know  someone just doesn't like and i think  i've always told myself  those people could also be going through  things and sometimes when  you know you're going through a really  hard time you feel alone  and you kind of want someone to feel  that too and you're like you know as  much as it it  it hurts and like you want to just let  someone feel it too because of how bad  it hurts and you want to be able to  get some of the pain off of yourself  it's just at the end of the day it's  such like a baggage to carry and i think  that  my advice for anyone out there that is  getting body shamed or going through  negative comments and stuff is just that  you know other people are going through  things and and you can't let that affect  you because you're beautiful you're  perfect and the way you are is  exactly how you're supposed to be and i  think at the end of the day every  imperfection you have makes you  completely unique  and it's something to really embrace and  just be like you know this is me this is  who i am  this is what makes me stand out and  different and then to the people that  that are the ones maybe putting the  negativity in the world i think it's  just  there are people that love you and that  are willing to talk to you and  and make your life better in any way  they can so always be open to talking to  someone and  if you can't trust you know a friend or  a family member there are plenty of  people that would be willing to  help you out and you are loved and  that's what i have to say about that
 

